# Conditional guidance

Some of this project's guidance applies CONDITIONALLY. Each entry gives a
fragment's NAME and the PREMISE under which it applies. Load any your
context does not already carry.

Match against WHAT YOU ARE ABOUT TO DO -- the next action, not the whole
conversation behind you. Take each premise ON ITS OWN and ask whether it
describes that action; you are not picking the single best match, and
several premises often apply at once.

When it is a BORDERLINE call, include it. An unnecessary fragment costs a
little context; one you withhold is never learned to exist and cannot be
asked for.

Select on the premise, not on the name. Then call the ctxloom
`assemble_context` tool with the names you chose (the `bundles` argument)
and follow what it returns.

- demo#fragments/golang: when editing Go code